# Server

# Firebase emulators (Auth + Firestore) — FILLED IN ON PURPOSE. Treat the three as one
# block: fill them all or empty them all.
# As shipped: `pnpm emulators` + `pnpm seed` + `pnpm dev` runs the whole stack locally,
# offline, with no Google account and without touching real data — and the service
# account below becomes unnecessary.
# To use a REAL Firebase project, EMPTY all three (VAR="") and fill in the service
# account. Running the emulators needs a JDK 21+ runtime. See docs/SETUP.md.
FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:8080"
FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:9099"
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID="demo-next-boilerplate"

# Firebase service account — required when the emulator hosts above are empty. It is how
# the API authenticates to Firestore (its database) and to Firebase Auth.
# Keep the newlines in the private key escaped as \n.
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PROJECT_ID=""
FIREBASE_ADMIN_CLIENT_EMAIL=""
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# Firebase Web API key — the API calls the Identity Toolkit REST endpoints with it
# (sign-in, sign-up, and confirming a password reset or an email verification).
# Found under Project settings > General > Web API Key.
FIREBASE_WEB_API_KEY=""

# Cloud Storage bucket (e.g. "my-project.firebasestorage.app"). OPTIONAL: without it the
# upload capability stays switched off — POST /files answers STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED and
# the panel shows the photo URL field instead of the file picker. Falls back to
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET when empty.
# Filling it in requires the Firebase Blaze plan, i.e. a payment method on file: Cloud
# Storage does not exist on Spark, where every call to a bucket answers 402/403. Real
# spend is still $0/month at MVP scale. Create the bucket in us-central1, us-east1 or
# us-west1 — they are the only regions with a free tier. See docs/PRE-PRODUCTION.md.
# Ignored while the emulator hosts above are filled in: Cloud Storage is not emulated, so
# honouring a bucket name there would write real objects into a real bucket.
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=""

# Comma-separated list of browser origins allowed to call the API. REQUIRED in
# production: the process refuses to start without it. Left empty outside production,
# the local front-ends below are assumed. There is no wildcard.
CORS_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001"

# Transactional email. Without both, password recovery does not exist: the reset
# request answers EMAIL_NOT_CONFIGURED instead of pretending to have sent a link.
# The sending domain needs SPF + DKIM verified at the provider.
RESEND_FROM=""
RESEND_TOKEN=""

# Stripe subscriptions. OPTIONAL: fill in both or neither. With either one empty, billing
# stays switched off: GET /payments/plans answers enabled=false and the panel keeps the
# "billing coming soon" placeholder, checkout and portal answer PAYMENTS_NOT_CONFIGURED,
# and the webhook answers 503 so Stripe retries instead of dropping events. Only one of
# the two filled in logs a [payments] warning at boot. Billing also needs
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL below and NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCT_MODE other than "simple".
# Register the webhook endpoint on API version 2025-09-30.clover with the events
# checkout.session.completed and customer.subscription.created/updated/deleted.
# See docs/PAYMENTS.md and docs/PRE-PRODUCTION.md.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# Optional. Without it, @repo/security degrades to a no-op: the public auth routes
# accept unlimited requests and the API says so once, at boot. That includes the
# password reset request and the verification resend, which then send mail unbounded.
ARCJET_KEY=""

VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL="http://localhost:3002"

# Client
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=""
# Base of the links sent in the account action emails (password reset, email
# verification). Must point at the real host of apps/app; without it the reset
# request answers EMAIL_NOT_CONFIGURED. Also the base Stripe sends people back to after
# checkout and the billing portal; without it billing stays switched off.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB_URL="http://localhost:3001"
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL="http://localhost:3004"
